TWO BUGS FOUND IN MY OWN WORK, both by the goldens:
1. SUBAGENT_FINISHED was emitted before the outgoing sub-agent's
   TEXT_MESSAGE_END, so its own content closed after it had finished.
2. Worse: on a root-to-subagent handover the ROOT's TEXT_MESSAGE_END was
   emitted after SUBAGENT_STARTED and stamped with the new run id. The
   plain-agent golden showed subagentRunId on an event authored by the
   root. Fixed by closing the outgoing producer's content before the
   handover, whoever it was, and pinned by
   TestSubagentHandoverDoesNotMisattribute.

PROCESS NOTE worth remembering: the first golden regeneration was done
while a temporary 'strip SUBAGENT_* events' proof was still active
(gofmt had reformatted the marker across lines so the revert missed it).
The result was a golden asserting the pre-subagent stream that passed
only because the normalizer hid the difference — a silently broken
golden. Caught by grepping the golden for subagent content rather than
trusting the green run. Regenerate goldens only from a verified-clean
normalizer, and check the regenerated content, not just the exit status.

